"edit_calls": 1, "ended_on_rejection": false, "error": null, "exec_mode": "local", "failure_class": "solved", "failure_reason": null, "faults_served": 0, "final_answer_complete": true, "final_answer_present": true, "final_answer_source": "json", "final_workspace": "/workspace/openbench-ab/results/step5-opus-aa-1017-omp36-aa/omp-36/cells/aa-1/trig-omp-reported/11/workspace", "first_after_build": false, "first_side": "aa-2", "fresh_subagents": 0, "harness": "omp", "harness_version": "omp/17.3.8 (/workspace/openbench-ab/results/omp-cache/bin/omp/5347ff91e8f44f2c69a79d7b152b7301687cd5c8/omp)", "harness_version_source": "host", "host": "grok-bot-vm-412615941", "image_digest": null, "last_activity_age_s": null, "list_has_generated": null, "main_agent_searched": false, "model": "claude-opus-5-5", "model_context_window": 1000000, "model_max_tokens": 128000, "output_tail": "Python 3.11+'s `datetime.fromisoformat` parses `Z` as UTC and keeps naive inputs naive, so it handles both cases.\n`test_dates` passes now. The bug was that `parse_date` used `strptime` with the fixed format `\"%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%S\"`, so it couldn't handle the trailing `Z` (UTC) in `\"2026-10-12T08:30:00Z\"`.\n\n**Fix** (`dates/parse.py`): I swapped it for `datetime.fromisoformat(s)`. On Python 3.11 and later this reads `Z` as UTC and still accepts timestamps with no zone. This machine runs Python 3.13.5, and I found no project config that pins an older version.\n\n`pytest tests/test_parse.py` now passes all 3 tests: `test_dates`, `test_naive` and `test_day_key`.\n\n**Behaviour changes to know about:**\n- **Timezone-aware results:** inputs ending in `Z` or `+HH:MM` now come back with a timezone attached (`tzinfo=UTC`), while inputs without a zone come back without one, as before. Python raises `TypeError` if you compare or subtract one kind against the other. Nothing in this repo does that; `day_key` only formats the result.\n- **Wider input:** `fromisoformat` also accepts other ISO-8601 forms, such as a date alone, fractional seconds or other offsets, which the old fixed format rejected.\n- **Older Python:** on Python 3.10 or earlier, `fromisoformat` rejects `Z`. If you need to support those versions, the code should turn the `Z` into `+00:00` before parsing.", "paced_wait_s": 0.0, "params_stripped": [], "params_stripped_requests": 0, "permission_rejections": 0, "read_calls": 2, "replies_ok": 8, "replies_throttled": 0, "requests_cache_read": 76757, "requests_cache_write": 133593, "requests_cost_usd": 0.7124883999999999, "requests_count": 8, "requests_input_uncached": 18, "requests_output": 1455, "reread": false, "rule_order": "none", "rule_prefix": "neither", "run_id": "omp:trig-omp-reported:claude-opus-5-5:trial11", "run_seed": 1016, "sampling_observed": null, "schedule_index": 21, "score": 1.0, "started_at": "2026-10-17T22:47:26.788530+00:00", "subagent_resumed": false, "subagent_write_calls": 0, "success": true, "t_agent_s": 30.572, "t_checker_s": 0.375, "t_env_setup_s": 0.001, "task": "trig-omp-reported", "task_calls": 0, "thinking_mode": "default", "thinking_sent": ["adaptive", "adaptive", "adaptive", "adaptive", "adaptive", "adaptive", "adaptive", "adaptive"], "timeout_s": 840, "tmpdir_leaked_dirs": 0, "token_basis": "proxy_measured", "token_basis_main": "estimated", "token_basis_proxy": "proxy_measured", "tokens": 1473, "tokens_cache_read": 76757, "tokens_cache_write": 133593, "tokens_fresh": 1473, "tokens_input_uncached": 18, "tokens_main_cache_read": 76757, "tokens_main_cache_write": 133593, "tokens_main_calls": 8, "tokens_main_input_uncached": 18, "tokens_main_output": 1455, "tokens_output": 1455, "tokens_proxy_cache_read": 76757, "tokens_proxy_cache_write": 133593, "tokens_proxy_calls": 8, "tokens_proxy_input_uncached": 18, "tokens_proxy_output": 1455, "tokens_proxy_reasoning": null, "tokens_reasoning": 0, "trial": 11, "ts_iso": "2026-10-17T18:47:26", "turn_mode": null, "turns": 8, "upstream_model": "claude-opus-5-5", "usage_raw": [{"cacheRead": 0, "cacheW